imperative programming techniques; control

18
00:01:26.908 --> 00:01:33.654
structures; problem solving using recursion;
basic searching and sorting; elementary data

19
00:01:33.654 --> 00:01:41.013
structures such as lists, trees, and graphs;
and correctness, testing and debugging.

20
00:01:41.013 --> 00:01:48.143
NARRATOR: Consider this worked case: A student
writes a pseudo code function for calculating

21
00:01:48.143 --> 00:01:54.763
