26
00:02:15.451 --> 00:02:22.177
NARRATOR: Separate the formal definition from
an implementation detail, then identify what

27
00:02:22.177 --> 00:02:24.419
evidence would distinguish them.

28
00:02:24.419 --> 00:02:30.966
NARRATOR: A precise definition makes later
examples easier to evaluate and revise.

29
00:02:31.082 --> 00:02:37.298
NARRATOR: With the foundation in place,
examine how Functional vs. Imperative

30
00:02:37.298 --> 00:02:40.688
Programming operates in a concrete sequence.

31
00:02:40.688 --> 00:02:46.860
NARRATOR: Dynamic programming records
solutions to overlapping subproblems.

32
00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:53.625
NARRATOR: Consider this worked case: A student
compares a recursive factorial function

33
00:02:53.625 --> 00:02:59.826
